1
00:02:05,892 --> 00:02:07,910
I think we just made some history.

2
00:02:16,450 --> 00:02:23,670
So, South Carolina, you have shown the nation what is possible.

3
00:02:24,756 --> 00:02:25,339
Possible.

4
00:02:25,339 --> 00:02:34,645
You have shown the nation that in this era of partisan divides, of vitriol and name-calling,

5
00:02:34,840 --> 00:02:42,763
In a politics dominated by billionaires and special interest groups and insiders in Washington D.C.

6
00:02:42,763 --> 00:02:44,620
That we will not bow down.

7
00:02:48,310 --> 00:02:53,150
That we will not back down and we will chart our own course.

8
00:02:54,886 --> 00:03:01,930
You have shown the nation that we can come together to defend South Carolina.

9
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:10,460
And today you have elected a senator that will always put South Carolina first.

10
00:03:16,190 --> 00:03:23,370
Not only that, but you have elected the first pediatrician to the United States Senate.

11
00:03:30,210 --> 00:03:30,550
That's right.

12
00:03:35,392 --> 00:03:41,382
The first woman that South Carolina has ever sent to the United States Senate.

13
00:03:49,120 --> 00:03:51,540
So, from the bottom of my heart, thank you.

14
00:03:52,720 --> 00:04:00,500
I want to start by thanking Darla Graham for her public service and her love for South Carolina,

15
00:04:01,140 --> 00:04:02,820
And I wish her her family well.

16
00:04:03,662 --> 00:04:10,200
And I just spoke with her and she congratulated me on our victory tonight.

17
00:04:17,580 --> 00:04:28,820
And to the heartbeat, the heartbeat of our campaign, our volunteers who worked their tails off and never stopped believing,

18
00:04:29,160 --> 00:04:30,820
Thank you, thank you, thank you.

19
00:04:31,828 --> 00:04:42,920
And to our state party chairwoman, Crystal Spain, the first black woman to lead our state's party,

20
00:04:47,600 --> 00:04:53,400
Who invested in this race, who believed in us, who believed in me and worked tirelessly,

21
00:04:53,760 --> 00:04:58,900
Tirelessly to build a stronger South Carolina across all 46 counties.

22
00:04:59,460 --> 00:05:04,184
Thank you, Crystal.

23
00:05:04,184 --> 00:05:07,530
And to my dear friend Jamie Harrison, we would not be here without you.

24
00:05:08,494 --> 00:05:09,330
Thank you so much.

25
00:05:13,360 --> 00:05:18,100
To all of our incredible staff who poured their hearts and souls into this race, Thank you.

26
00:05:20,720 --> 00:05:24,880
To the thousands of people who welcomed us into their homes, their churches,

27
00:05:25,100 --> 00:05:28,880
Their businesses, and onto their front porches, thank you so much.

28
00:05:30,123 --> 00:05:38,300
And to the Republicans, Independents, and Democrats who took a chance on a pediatrician and a mom of three,

29
00:05:38,300 --> 00:05:46,820
Because you believed that South Carolina should come first, thank you.

30
00:05:49,590 --> 00:05:53,990
South Carolina, my name may have been on the ballot, but this victory doesn't belong to me,

31
00:05:54,150 --> 00:05:55,530
It belongs to all of you.

32
00:05:56,324 --> 00:06:05,730
Because tonight we here in South Carolina sent a clear message that this Senate seat does not belong to one family,

33
00:06:06,310 --> 00:06:09,010
One party, or to Washington DC.

34
00:06:15,990 --> 00:06:18,810
It belongs to you and it always will.

35
00:06:19,630 --> 00:06:27,510
We embarked on this journey over 18 months ago and while it was long and exhausting and there were plenty of days when I

36
00:06:27,510 --> 00:06:31,970
Was running on nothing but protein bars, coffee, and giant Diet Cokes from gas stations,

37
00:06:32,530 --> 00:06:35,110
It truly has been the journey of a lifetime.

38
00:06:35,810 --> 00:06:42,870
We took this campaign to every single one of our 46 counties from small towns and main streets to farms and our rural communities

39
00:06:42,870 --> 00:06:47,770
From the Blue Ridge Mountains in the upstate to the swamps, the literal swamps in the Midlands,

40
00:06:47,770 --> 00:06:50,410
To the beaches here in the Low Country.

41
00:06:51,344 --> 00:07:02,983
I sat on the back of a pickup truck with an eighth generation farmer in Barnwell who told me that it now costs her $1,900.

42
00:07:32,395 --> 00:07:34,500
Y'all, I thought my farmer friend was here.

43
00:07:36,400 --> 00:07:43,482
She told me it cost $1,900 to fill up her tractor with diesel and that tank of gas will only last her for 3 Days.

44
00:07:43,608 --> 00:07:50,300
And that farm that's been in her South Carolina family for eight generations might not last another year or two if things don't change.

45
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:57,280
I've stood shoulder to shoulder with veterans in Ridgeland, tears in their eyes as they told me that they've lost friends to suicide,

46
00:07:57,600 --> 00:08:04,660
That their fight for their benefits that they've earned and their fear of another generation being sent off to a reckless war.

47
00:08:04,660 --> 00:08:13,290
I've spoken to seniors who've worked their entire lives, raised their family, and did everything right,

48
00:08:13,290 --> 00:08:17,310
Only to find themselves struggling to get by on their Social Security checks.

49
00:08:17,790 --> 00:08:24,490
I've seen neighbors looking out for each other regardless of political party, families coming together to help each other through hard times,

50
00:08:24,490 --> 00:08:30,050
And church congregations opening their hearts and doors to anyone who needs a helping hand.

51
00:08:30,905 --> 00:08:32,830
This is the South Carolina that I know.

52
00:08:33,150 --> 00:08:36,410
This is the South Carolina that I am proud to call home.

53
00:08:41,860 --> 00:08:47,560
And this is the South Carolina that I will fight for every single day in the United States Senate.

54
00:08:48,591 --> 00:08:58,810
And to the South Carolinians who did not vote for me, I know we may not agree on everything,

55
00:08:58,810 --> 00:09:03,190
And I may not have earned your vote today, but I want you to know this,

56
00:09:03,190 --> 00:09:05,270
I will be your senator too.

57
00:09:09,260 --> 00:09:15,280
I will listen to you, I will show up for you, and I will fight just as hard for you and your children as

58
00:09:15,280 --> 00:09:16,620
I would my own.

59
00:09:17,280 --> 00:09:18,880
That's the kind of senator that I'll be.

60
00:09:22,870 --> 00:09:26,490
I'll be an independent voice who will work with anyone, Republican or Democrat,

61
00:09:26,490 --> 00:09:28,310
To do what's right for South Carolina.

62
00:09:29,030 --> 00:09:31,550
I will be a brick wall between Washington D.C.

63
00:09:31,550 --> 00:09:35,150
And South Carolina, even when it means standing up to my own party.

64
00:09:38,310 --> 00:09:41,730
Nobody in Washington recruited me to run.

65
00:09:44,460 --> 00:09:48,820
Nobody handed me a seat in the United States Senate.

66
00:09:51,580 --> 00:09:53,640
And nobody wrote me a script.

67
00:09:54,620 --> 00:09:59,160
I owe no one in Washington anything.

68
00:09:59,520 --> 00:10:02,000
I owe South Carolina everything.

69
00:10:06,890 --> 00:10:09,670
And that's exactly who I'm going to answer to.

70
00:10:09,670 --> 00:10:12,750
Now, I never imagined that I would end up in politics.

71
00:10:12,750 --> 00:10:18,370
Since I was four, I've only ever dreamed of becoming a doctor, and for the past 20 years,

72
00:10:18,690 --> 00:10:21,710
I've dedicated my life to caring for sick and injured children.

73
00:10:22,310 --> 00:10:28,710
But what I saw as a pediatrician and what I've experienced raising my own three children made me realize that I couldn't just sit

74
00:10:28,710 --> 00:10:29,890
On the sidelines anymore.

75
00:10:30,430 --> 00:10:35,010
I watched as insurance companies stood between sick children and the care that they need.

76
00:10:35,010 --> 00:10:40,830
I've seen how decisions made in Washington affect the lives of the children and families I've cared for.

77
00:10:41,290 --> 00:10:48,830
And that's why I decided to run, because I believe we have a responsibility to leave our children something better than what we inherited.

78
00:10:49,767 --> 00:10:55,700
A South Carolina where a family can afford to fill up a gas tank,

79
00:10:55,820 --> 00:11:01,280
Put groceries on the table, and get the child care they need without worrying about going broke.

80
00:11:01,998 --> 00:11:07,020
When decisions where decisions about our communities are made by the people who live in our communities,

81
00:11:07,200 --> 00:11:10,340
Not the billionaires or data center companies in Washington DC.

82
00:11:13,710 --> 00:11:18,110
And where the next generation can afford to build a life and raise a family here.

83
00:11:18,290 --> 00:11:20,050
That's the future that I'm fighting for.

84
00:11:23,570 --> 00:11:30,390
And I know that the work ahead won't be easy, but after 18 months and 46 counties and everything we've been through together,

85
00:11:30,630 --> 00:11:33,130
I've never been more certain of one thing.

86
00:11:33,979 --> 00:11:37,410
South Carolina's best days are still ahead of US.

87
00:11:59,398 --> 00:12:02,940
And I promise you I'm going to give you everything I have to make sure we get there.

88
00:12:03,060 --> 00:12:07,780
To build a South Carolina you can afford, a South Carolina you can always be proud to call home,

89
00:12:07,780 --> 00:12:10,560
And a South Carolina that will always come first.

90
00:12:11,160 --> 00:12:12,740
So thank you for believing in me.

91
00:12:13,260 --> 00:12:16,280
Thank you for making history with me tonight.

92
00:12:17,199 --> 00:12:22,560
And and most importantly, we had to move this part to the end so I wouldn't be a blubbering idiot up here.

93
00:12:22,560 --> 00:12:25,580
Most importantly, thank you to my family.

94
00:12:31,090 --> 00:12:34,870
To my parents who have stood by me every step of the way.

95
00:12:37,290 --> 00:12:39,210
And to my three children.

96
00:12:46,780 --> 00:12:50,660
Thank you for every hug, every word of encouragement.

97
00:12:52,120 --> 00:12:57,780
I love you more than words Henry than words will ever express.

98
00:12:58,600 --> 00:12:59,620
I'm so proud of you guys.

99
00:13:02,733 --> 00:13:10,410
And being your mom will always be the most important job I have.

100
00:13:12,559 --> 00:13:16,289
All right.

101
00:13:16,299 --> 00:13:17,789
All right.

102
00:13:17,789 --> 00:13:21,330
And I hope that when you look back on this moment, all three of you,

103
00:13:21,330 --> 00:13:22,770
I hope that you remember something.

104
00:13:23,390 --> 00:13:26,010
That you can stand up for what you believe in.

105
00:13:26,270 --> 00:13:29,530
That you can speak out when something isn't right.

106
00:13:30,850 --> 00:13:36,070
And no matter how big the challenge, you should never be afraid to try to make things better.

107
00:13:41,310 --> 00:13:45,220
Because you never know what's possible if you're willing to try.

108
00:13:50,400 --> 00:13:53,440
South Carolina, I love you.

109
00:13:53,860 --> 00:13:56,380
Thank you and good night.
